<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Urmia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rezaiyeh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Urmia is a city in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, the capital of West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> province, on a plain west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-urmia">Lake Urmia</a>. Long home to Muslims alongside Assyrian and Armenian Christians, it was a centre of Christian missions in the 19th century. After 1747 it was the seat of a khanate of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afshar-tribe">Afshar tribe</a>, absorbed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajar</a> Iran in the 1790s. It suffered severely during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/urmia.jpg" alt="Urmia" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ✿ Vlinder · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uromia_Iran,pareeke_jangali_-_panoramio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
